Homepage: https://github.com/vomlehn/tcspecial
Description: telemetry and control, special: spacecraft flight software
 tcspecial runs a spacecraft's payloads as nodes in a configured graph and
 relays their data and commands to and from the mission operations center
 over UDP. This package is what flies: tcspecial itself, tcsverify,
 which checks a configuration, the five test app programs under
 /opt/tcs/libexec, the manual, and the example configurations. Everything
 is under /opt/tcs. /etc/profile.d/tcspecial.sh puts /opt/tcs/bin on a
 login shell's search path, and /opt/tcs/sbin/tcspecial-links links the
 programs into /usr/local/bin for everything else.
 A configuration that keeps a telemetry log needs a segsend beside
 tcspecial: the mission's own, or the test one in tcspecial-test.
 .
 A systemd unit, tcspecial.service, is installed but not enabled: it runs
 /opt/tcs/bin/tcspecial on /etc/opt/tcs/tcspecial/tcspecial.yaml once
 one is put there, and starts it again whenever it exits.
